# SonarCloud constraints

SonarCloud runs on CI. Write code that already passes these checks.

- Keep cognitive complexity at or below 15. Extract a helper when a function nests loops, conditions, or boolean chains.
- Define a function at module scope when it does not use variables from the enclosing function.
- Alphabetical `sort` and `toSorted` must take a compare function that uses `String.localeCompare` (typescript:S2871). Do not call either with no comparer. Sort numbers with a numeric comparer.
- Do not pass `unknown` or `object` values to `String()`. Narrow with `typeof value === 'string'` first.
- Compare with `undefined` directly instead of `typeof x === 'undefined'` (typescript:S7741). Reserve `typeof` for a binding that may not exist, such as `window` during server render.
- Use `??` when the only fallback is `null` or `undefined`.
- Import snapshot types from `src/types/snapshot.ts`. Do not re-export them from the file that uses them.
- Do not use `Math.random()` for tokens, secrets, session ids, passwords, or nonces (typescript:S2245). Use `crypto.randomUUID()` or `crypto.getRandomValues()`. `Math.random()` is only acceptable for non-security values such as UI jitter or demo data.
- Prefer `Number` static methods and properties over the global equivalents (typescript:S7773): `Number.parseInt`, `Number.parseFloat`, `Number.isNaN`, `Number.isFinite`, `Number.NaN`, `Number.POSITIVE_INFINITY`, and `Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY`.
- Every `<label>` needs accessible text and an associated control (Web:S6853). Set `for` to the control `id`, or wrap the control. Text, `aria-label`, or `aria-labelledby` must name the label.
- Every `<input>`, `<select>`, and `<textarea>` needs a label (Web:InputWithoutLabelCheck). Give the control an `id` and point a `<label for>` at it, wrap it in a `<label>`, or set `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby`.
- Do not set `aria-hidden="true"` on a focusable element (Web:S6825): links, buttons, inputs, selects, textareas, `contenteditable`, or anything with `tabindex` of 0 or more. Put `aria-hidden` on a decorative child, such as an icon, instead of the control.
- Keep regular expressions linear (typescript:S8786). Do not nest quantifiers or overlap alternatives that can match the same text, such as `(a+)+` or `(a|aa)+`. Use one quantifier or a negated character class.
- Use a collection's contents or do not create it (typescript:S4030). Do not build an array, set, or map that is never read. Use `forEach` or a loop for side effects, and keep the result of `map`, `filter`, `slice`, and `concat`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
return typeof window.localStorage === 'undefined' ? null : window.localStorage
return names.sort()
return names.toSorted()
const sessionId = Math.random().toString(36)
const port = parseInt(raw, 10)
const letters = /^(a+)+$/
names.map((name) => name.toLowerCase())

// ✅ GOOD
return window.localStorage ?? null
return names.sort((left, right) => left.localeCompare(right))
return names.toSorted((left, right) => left.localeCompare(right))
const sessionId = crypto.randomUUID()
const port = Number.parseInt(raw, 10)
const letters = /^a+$/
const normalized = names.map((name) => name.toLowerCase())
```

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<label></label>
<label>Route</label>
<input type="text" />
<select></select>
<textarea></textarea>
<button type="button" aria-hidden="true">Close</button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<label for="route-filter">Route</label>
<input id="route-filter" type="text" />
<label for="span-type">Span type</label>
<select id="span-type"></select>
<label for="trace-notes">Notes</label>
<textarea id="trace-notes"></textarea>
<button type="button">
    <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
    Close
</button>
```
